RedwoodGPU publishes NegroniGPUABI, so Turnip's drm layer uses host import (0x49).

all35 (m2vtest): "host import of ...: not a noted IOSurface, and no USERPTR (kernel without
0232)", then metal2vulkan "no-copy buffer: Unsupported HostMemory": negroni_drm.c sends 0x49 only
when the service's NegroniGPUABI text names "userptr". Our kernel has 0x49 since 0156.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/RedwoodGPU.cpp
@@ -365,6 +365,12 @@
 		return false;
 	}
 	setProperty(kIOUserClientClassKey, "RedwoodGPUUserClient");
+	/*
+	 * What Turnip's libdrm stand-in (iOSPlus10 negronigl drm/negroni_drm.c) reads to learn the
+	 * requests here: no "userptr" in it and it never sends 0x49 (all35: "no USERPTR (kernel without
+	 * 0232)", so metal2vulkan's no-copy buffers were refused). msm requests only, one address space.
+	 */
+	setProperty("NegroniGPUABI", "msm 0x09 0x40-0x4c 0x7e, userptr 0x49, va shared");
 	setName("RedwoodGPU");
 	registerService();
 	return true;
